IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pta-small-estates`

-- Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask about the Public Trustee and an estate, with
-- the seat and the situation as parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The Act speaks almost entirely to the Public Trustee and the Court; the baseline (pta-small-estates.l4) asked
-- its questions from the seat of the next of kin of a person who has died leaving a small estate, and, for ss 7-8, of
-- the will-maker. Here four people ask:
--   - the next of kin of a person who has died: the baseline's main seat (all 17 of its questions);
--   - a person making a will, or who has made one: ss 2(c), 7(1), 8 and 47A (the baseline's will-maker seat);
--   - a beneficiary of an estate or trust the Public Trustee administers: a client under s 2(a), (e), who asks about
--     fees (ss 9, 38A, 38B, 62) and unclaimed money (s 45);
--   - a creditor of the person who died, whom s 11 sets against the Public Trustee.
-- The Public Trustee and the Court are never seats: what they may or must do appears as what it means for the person
-- asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when the
-- situation does not hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, with the
-- same name, type and @desc, so the form asks it once. There is one, for the next of kin:
--   - `the Public Trustee's part in the estate` (`The Public Trustee's part`): none yet; a small-estate election filed
--     (s 14); administering under an order, a grant or as executor. s 14(4) and (5) speak "after filing such election",
--     so their two questions arise only for the election; the child's share (s 18, "administration has been granted to
--     the Public Trustee", which s 14(2) deems the election to be), the fees (ss 9, 38A, 38B, 62) and the unclaimed
--     balance (s 45, sums "held by the Public Trustee") arise only once the Public Trustee has the estate, by either
--     route. The questions of whether the Public Trustee may take the estate on (ss 10, 11, 12, 14(1), 10(4), 8) arise in
--     every situation and take no situation input. Since s 18 arises only once the Public Trustee holds the grant (or the
--     election deemed one), the layer passes the baseline's `the Public Trustee holds the grant` as TRUE instead of
--     asking it again.
-- The will-maker, the beneficiary (whose role already says the Public Trustee administers) and the creditor have no
-- situation input.
--
-- The rules are in pta-small-estates.l4. This module calls them and restates none; for the next of kin and the
-- will-maker each answer is the baseline export's own answer, wrapped. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT
-- input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am next of kin of someone who has died`
    `I am making a will, or have made one`
    `I am a beneficiary of an estate or trust the Public Trustee administers`
    `I am owed money by someone who has died`

DECLARE `The Public Trustee's part` IS ONE OF
    `none yet`
    `it has filed a small-estate election (s 14)`
    `it administers the estate under an order to administer, a grant, or as executor`

-- The estate and the family, as the next of kin is asked them (fix of 6 November 2026; NOTES.md QA-5). The site's form
-- drops a question for a role it is not about only by trying every combination of its open yes/no and choice inputs, at
-- most 1,024 of them. With the baseline's `The estate`, `The family` and `What the Court thinks` the s 10(1) and s 14(1)
-- questions had 12 yes/no facts, 4,096 combinations. Five of them say one thing, whether there is a will and who will
-- act on it: `the deceased left a will`, `an executor named in the will is willing, capable and resident in WA`, `the
-- person first entitled to administration is willing, capable and resident in WA` (s 10(1)(ab), an intestacy), `the
-- executor renounced and everyone first entitled declined in writing filed in Court` (s 10(1)(b), a will) and `the will
-- expressly prohibits the executor authorising the Public Trustee` (s 12(2), a will). The layer asks them as one choice
-- of eight, `The will and who will act`, and builds the baseline's records from it; the facts the baseline's rules do
-- not read in a value (the executor with no will; the person first entitled with a will) are given fixed values that
-- change no answer. The questions now have 1,024 combinations at most.
DECLARE `The will and who will act` IS ONE OF
    `no will; the person first entitled to administration is willing, capable and resident in WA`
    `no will; the person first entitled to administration is unwilling, incapable or not resident in WA`
    `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA`
    `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee`
    `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA`
    `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee`
    `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court`
    `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee`

DECLARE `The estate, as the next of kin knows it` HAS
    `the person who died left property in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they left property outside Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gross value in WA, as the Public Trustee estimates it` IS A NUMBER
    `probate or administration has been taken out in WA` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days since they died` IS A NUMBER
    `full months since they died` IS A NUMBER
    `the will and who will act` IS A `The will and who will act`

DECLARE `What the family is doing` HAS
    `the estate is unprotected or liable to waste, and the family absent or not found` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the estate is perishable, or in danger of being lost or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how many persons are entitled to obtain administration` IS A NUMBER
    `how many of them have authorised the Public Trustee to apply` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Ground answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the ground` IS A `Ground for the Public Trustee`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The situation helpers list every value and have no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31: a CONSIDER with OTHERWISE takes
-- the OTHERWISE branch for an ASSUMEd value instead of failing, so a case could not show the value was not read).
GIVEN `the part` IS A `The Public Trustee's part`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Trustee has not filed an election` IF
    CONSIDER `the part`
    WHEN `none yet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it has filed a small-estate election (s 14)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `it administers the estate under an order to administer, a grant, or as executor` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `the part` IS A `The Public Trustee's part`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Trustee has no part in the estate` IF
    CONSIDER `the part`
    WHEN `none yet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it has filed a small-estate election (s 14)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `it administers the estate under an order to administer, a grant, or as executor` THEN FALSE

-- What each value of `The will and who will act` says, for the baseline's records. Every value is listed, with no
-- OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `the will` IS A `The will and who will act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a will` IF
    CONSIDER `the will`
    WHEN `no will; the person first entitled to administration is willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no will; the person first entitled to administration is unwilling, incapable or not resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `the will` IS A `The will and who will act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an executor is willing, capable and resident in WA` IF
    CONSIDER `the will`
    WHEN `no will; the person first entitled to administration is willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no will; the person first entitled to administration is unwilling, incapable or not resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the will` IS A `The will and who will act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person first entitled is willing, capable and resident in WA` IF
    CONSIDER `the will`
    WHEN `no will; the person first entitled to administration is willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `no will; the person first entitled to administration is unwilling, incapable or not resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `the will` IS A `The will and who will act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the executor renounced and those first entitled declined` IF
    CONSIDER `the will`
    WHEN `no will; the person first entitled to administration is willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no will; the person first entitled to administration is unwilling, incapable or not resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `the will` IS A `The will and who will act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the will forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` IF
    CONSIDER `the will`
    WHEN `no will; the person first entitled to administration is willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no will; the person first entitled to administration is unwilling, incapable or not resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will, with an executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will, with no executor willing, capable and resident in WA, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a will whose executor renounced probate, those first entitled having declined in writing filed in Court, that forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `the estate` IS A `The estate, as the next of kin knows it`
GIVETH AN `The estate`
`the estate as the Act puts it` `the estate` MEANS
    `The estate` WITH
        `left property in Western Australia`                                   IS `the estate`'s `the person who died left property in Western Australia`
        `left property outside Western Australia`                              IS `the estate`'s `they left property outside Western Australia`
        `gross value in Western Australia as estimated by the Public Trustee`  IS `the estate`'s `the gross value in WA, as the Public Trustee estimates it`
        `the deceased left a will`                                             IS `there is a will` (`the estate`'s `the will and who will act`)
        `someone has taken out probate or administration in Western Australia` IS `the estate`'s `probate or administration has been taken out in WA`
        `days since the death`                                                 IS `the estate`'s `days since they died`
        `full months since the death`                                          IS `the estate`'s `full months since they died`

GIVEN `the estate` IS A `The estate, as the next of kin knows it`
      `the family` IS A `What the family is doing`
GIVETH A `The family`
`the family as the Act puts it` `the estate` `the family` MEANS
    `The family` WITH
        `an executor named in the will is willing, capable and resident in WA`                 IS `an executor is willing, capable and resident in WA` (`the estate`'s `the will and who will act`)
        `the person first entitled to administration is willing, capable and resident in WA`   IS `the person first entitled is willing, capable and resident in WA` (`the estate`'s `the will and who will act`)
        `the executor renounced and everyone first entitled declined in writing filed in Court` IS `the executor renounced and those first entitled declined` (`the estate`'s `the will and who will act`)
        `the estate is unprotected or liable to waste and the family is absent or not found`   IS `the family`'s `the estate is unprotected or liable to waste, and the family absent or not found`
        `the estate is perishable or in danger of being lost or destroyed`                     IS `the family`'s `the estate is perishable, or in danger of being lost or destroyed`
        `persons entitled to obtain administration`                                            IS `the family`'s `how many persons are entitled to obtain administration`
        `of them, persons who have authorised the Public Trustee to apply`                     IS `the family`'s `how many of them have authorised the Public Trustee to apply`
        `the will expressly prohibits the executor authorising the Public Trustee`             IS `the will forbids the executor to authorise the Public Trustee` (`the estate`'s `the will and who will act`)

-- s 47A(1)-(2), for the will-maker: the charge the baseline's enumeration names, from whether a legal practitioner
-- directs and controls the preparation.
GIVEN `a legal practitioner directs it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What the charge is for`
`the will preparation charge` `a legal practitioner directs it` MEANS
    IF `a legal practitioner directs it`
    THEN `a will prepared under a legal practitioner's direction and control`
    ELSE `a will prepared without a legal practitioner's direction and control`

§§ `For the next of kin of someone who has died`

§§§ `ss 10(1), 11, 12 -- may the Public Trustee take the estate on`

@export May we authorise the Public Trustee to apply to administer the estate (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 12(1)-(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the estate` IS AN `The estate, as the next of kin knows it` @desc The deceased's estate, whether there is a will, and who will act
      `the family` IS A `What the family is doing` @desc What the family is doing, and who has authorised the Public Trustee
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May we authorise the Public Trustee to apply` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN `yes if` (`Have we authorised the Public Trustee to apply` (`the estate as the Act puts it` `the estate`) (`the family as the Act puts it` `the estate` `the family`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export On what ground, if any, may the Public Trustee apply for an order to administer the estate (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 10(1), s 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the estate` IS AN `The estate, as the next of kin knows it` @desc The deceased's estate, whether there is a will, and who will act
      `the family` IS A `What the family is doing` @desc What the family is doing, and who has authorised the Public Trustee
      `the Court` IS A `What the Court thinks` @desc The Court's view on the matters s 10(1)(d) and (g) leave to it
GIVETH A `Ground answer`
`On what ground may the Public Trustee apply, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN `the answer is` (`On what ground may the Public Trustee apply` (`the estate as the Act puts it` `the estate`) (`the family as the Act puts it` `the estate` `the family`) `the Court`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the Public Trustee apply for an order to administer the estate (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 10(1), s 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the estate` IS AN `The estate, as the next of kin knows it` @desc The deceased's estate, whether there is a will, and who will act
      `the family` IS A `What the family is doing` @desc What the family is doing, and who has authorised the Public Trustee
      `the Court` IS A `What the Court thinks` @desc The Court's view on the matters s 10(1)(d) and (g) leave to it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Public Trustee apply for an order to administer, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN `yes if` (`May the Public Trustee apply for an order to administer` (`the estate as the Act puts it` `the estate`) (`the family as the Act puts it` `the estate` `the family`) `the Court`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If the Public Trustee relies on s 10(1)(ab), may the Court grant administration to me instead because I live in WA and have applied (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 10(1)(ab))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I live in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in the State
      `I would otherwise be entitled to administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would be entitled to administration but for s 10(1)(ab)
      `I have applied for administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Court grant administration to me instead, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN `yes if` (`May the Court grant administration to me instead` `I live in Western Australia` `I would otherwise be entitled to administration` `I have applied for administration`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the Public Trustee preferred to a creditor who applies to administer the estate (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the creditor proves to the Court it would be more beneficial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied the creditor administering would benefit the estate more
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the Public Trustee preferred to a creditor, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN `yes if` (`Is the Public Trustee preferred to a creditor` `the creditor proves to the Court it would be more beneficial`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 10(4), 14 -- the small-estate election, without any grant`

@export May the Public Trustee administer the estate without any grant, by filing a small-estate election, the estate being worth no more than $50 000 (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 14(1); Trustee Companies Regulations 1988 reg 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the estate` IS AN `The estate, as the next of kin knows it` @desc The deceased's estate, whether there is a will, and who will act
      `the family` IS A `What the family is doing` @desc What the family is doing, and who has authorised the Public Trustee
      `the Court` IS A `What the Court thinks` @desc The Court's view on the matters s 10(1)(d) and (g) leave to it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Public Trustee administer without a grant, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN `yes if` (`May the Public Trustee administer without a grant` (`the estate as the Act puts it` `the estate`) (`the family as the Act puts it` `the estate` `the family`) `the Court`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export After its small-estate election, must the Public Trustee go to the Court for an order after all (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 14(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Public Trustee's part in the estate` IS A `The Public Trustee's part` @desc Whether the Public Trustee has any part in the estate yet: none, a small-estate election filed, or administering it under an order, a grant or as executor
      `the gross value found` IS A NUMBER @desc The gross value of the property to be administered, as found after the election, in dollars
      `property outside WA has been found` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the property turns out to include property outside Western Australia
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Public Trustee seek an order after all, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `the Public Trustee has not filed an election` `the Public Trustee's part in the estate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must the Public Trustee seek an order after all` `the gross value found` `property outside WA has been found`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If a will turns up after the Public Trustee elected to administer an estate thought intestate, must the election be revoked and accounts filed (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 14(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Public Trustee's part in the estate` IS A `The Public Trustee's part` @desc Whether the Public Trustee has any part in the estate yet: none, a small-estate election filed, or administering it under an order, a grant or as executor
      `the election treated the deceased as intestate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the election was made on the footing that there was no will
      `a will has been found` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Public Trustee has found that the deceased left a will
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the election be revoked and accounts filed, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `the Public Trustee has not filed an election` `the Public Trustee's part in the estate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must the election be revoked and accounts filed` `the election treated the deceased as intestate` `a will has been found`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Where everyone who held the grant has died and part of the estate is left unadministered, may the Public Trustee finish it by election, without a new grant (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 10(4)-(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `every grantee has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether everyone to whom probate or administration was granted has died
      `gross value left unadministered` IS A NUMBER @desc The Public Trustee's estimate of the unadministered part, in dollars
      `a grant de bonis non has been taken out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone has taken out letters of administration de bonis non since
      `the Public Trustee is entitled to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Public Trustee could apply for an order to administer
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Public Trustee finish the estate by election, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN `yes if` (`May the Public Trustee finish the estate by election` `every grantee has died` `gross value left unadministered` `a grant de bonis non has been taken out` `the Public Trustee is entitled to apply`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 2, 7, 8 -- the Public Trustee as executor, and who is a client`

@export May the Public Trustee act as executor of my relative's will and obtain probate (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) ss 7-8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the will or a codicil names the Public Trustee as executor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Public Trustee is named as executor in the will or a codicil
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Public Trustee act as executor of my relative's will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN `yes if` (`May the Public Trustee act as executor` `the will or a codicil names the Public Trustee as executor`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I a client of the Public Trustee (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 2)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my dealing` IS A `My dealing with the Public Trustee` @desc How you deal with the Public Trustee
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I a client of the Public Trustee, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN `yes if` (`Am I a client of the Public Trustee` `my dealing`)
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`Am I a client of the Public Trustee` `my dealing`)
    WHEN `I am a beneficiary of an estate or trust the Public Trustee administers` THEN `yes if` (`Am I a client of the Public Trustee` `my dealing`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 18 -- a child's small share`

@export May the Public Trustee pay my child's share of the estate to me, as parent or carer (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 18)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Public Trustee's part in the estate` IS A `The Public Trustee's part` @desc Whether the Public Trustee has any part in the estate yet: none, a small-estate election filed, or administering it under an order, a grant or as executor
      `the net amount payable to the child` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's net share, in dollars
      `I am a parent or have care or custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the child's parent or have the child's care or custody
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Public Trustee pay my child's share to me, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `the Public Trustee has no part in the estate` `the Public Trustee's part in the estate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May the Public Trustee pay my child's share to me` TRUE `the net amount payable to the child` `I am a parent or have care or custody`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 9, 38A, 38B, 47A, 62 -- what the Public Trustee may charge`

@export May the Public Trustee charge the estate or me for this (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) ss 9, 38B, 47A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Public Trustee's part in the estate` IS A `The Public Trustee's part` @desc Whether the Public Trustee has any part in the estate yet: none, a small-estate election filed, or administering it under an order, a grant or as executor
      `the charge` IS A `What the charge is for` @desc What the fee, commission or charge is for
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Public Trustee charge for this, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `the Public Trustee has no part in the estate` `the Public Trustee's part in the estate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May the Public Trustee charge for this` `the charge`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most the Public Trustee may take from the estate in fees and expenses (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) ss 38A, 38B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Public Trustee's part in the estate` IS A `The Public Trustee's part` @desc Whether the Public Trustee has any part in the estate yet: none, a small-estate election filed, or administering it under an order, a grant or as executor
      `the fees` IS A `The fee facts` @desc The scale, any directed or agreed fee, expenses and any waiver
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most the Public Trustee may charge, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `the Public Trustee has no part in the estate` `the Public Trustee's part in the estate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`What is the most the Public Trustee may charge` `the fees`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Are the Public Trustee's fees paid out of the estate, as a testamentary expense, rather than by me personally (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) ss 38B(4), 62)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Public Trustee's part in the estate` IS A `The Public Trustee's part` @desc Whether the Public Trustee has any part in the estate yet: none, a small-estate election filed, or administering it under an order, a grant or as executor
      `the fee is for administering the estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fee is charged for the administration or management of the estate
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Are the fees paid out of the estate, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `the Public Trustee has no part in the estate` `the Public Trustee's part in the estate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Are the fees paid out of the estate` `the fee is for administering the estate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 45 -- an unclaimed balance and the State`

@export Must the Public Trustee advertise an unclaimed estate balance, twice 14 days apart in a Perth newspaper, before it goes to the State (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 45(2); Public Trustee Regulations 1942 reg 10A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Public Trustee's part in the estate` IS A `The Public Trustee's part` @desc Whether the Public Trustee has any part in the estate yet: none, a small-estate election filed, or administering it under an order, a grant or as executor
      `the sum` IS A NUMBER @desc The unclaimed sum to the credit of the estate, in dollars
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Public Trustee advertise the unclaimed sum, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `the Public Trustee has no part in the estate` `the Public Trustee's part in the estate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must the Public Trustee advertise the unclaimed sum` `the sum`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the estate money held for me be paid to the State's Consolidated Account as unclaimed (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 45(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Public Trustee's part in the estate` IS A `The Public Trustee's part` @desc Whether the Public Trustee has any part in the estate yet: none, a small-estate election filed, or administering it under an order, a grant or as executor
      `years the sum has been held` IS A NUMBER @desc Years the sum has been held to the credit of the estate before 1 March
      `the Public Trustee knows of someone entitled or claiming` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Public Trustee has any information of a person entitled in distribution, or claiming to be
      `the sum` IS A NUMBER @desc The unclaimed sum to the credit of the estate, in dollars
      `it has been advertised twice 14 days apart` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has been advertised as s 45(2) requires
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the sum go to the Consolidated Account, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am next of kin of someone who has died` THEN
        IF `the Public Trustee has no part in the estate` `the Public Trustee's part in the estate`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May the sum go to the Consolidated Account` `years the sum has been held` `the Public Trustee knows of someone entitled or claiming` `the sum` `it has been advertised twice 14 days apart`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a person making a will, or who has made one`

§§§ `ss 7, 8 -- naming the Public Trustee as executor`

@export If my will names the Public Trustee as executor, may it act and obtain probate (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) ss 7(1), 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my will names the Public Trustee as executor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your will or a codicil names the Public Trustee as executor
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Public Trustee act as executor of my will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`May the Public Trustee act as executor` `my will names the Public Trustee as executor`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 47A -- a fee for preparing my will`

@export May the Public Trustee charge me a fee for preparing my will (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 47A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a legal practitioner directs and controls the preparation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the will is prepared under the direction and control of a legal practitioner
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Public Trustee charge me for preparing my will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a will, or have made one` THEN `yes if` (`May the Public Trustee charge for this` (`the will preparation charge` `a legal practitioner directs and controls the preparation`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a beneficiary of an estate or trust the Public Trustee administers`

§§§ `ss 9, 38A, 38B, 62 -- fees`

@export May the Public Trustee charge the estate for this (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) ss 9, 38B, 47A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the charge` IS A `What the charge is for` @desc What the fee, commission or charge is for
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Public Trustee charge the estate I benefit from for this` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a beneficiary of an estate or trust the Public Trustee administers` THEN `yes if` (`May the Public Trustee charge for this` `the charge`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most the Public Trustee may take in fees and expenses from the estate I benefit from (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) ss 38A, 38B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the fees` IS A `The fee facts` @desc The scale, any directed or agreed fee, expenses and any waiver
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most the Public Trustee may take from the estate I benefit from` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a beneficiary of an estate or trust the Public Trustee administers` THEN amount (`What is the most the Public Trustee may charge` `the fees`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Are the Public Trustee's fees paid out of the estate, as a testamentary expense, rather than out of my share by me personally (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) ss 38B(4), 62)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the fee is for administering the estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fee is charged for the administration or management of the estate
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Are the fees paid out of the estate I benefit from` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a beneficiary of an estate or trust the Public Trustee administers` THEN `yes if` (`Are the fees paid out of the estate` `the fee is for administering the estate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 45 -- money held for me and not claimed`

@export May money the Public Trustee holds for me be paid to the State's Consolidated Account as unclaimed (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 45; Public Trustee Regulations 1942 reg 10A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `years the sum has been held` IS A NUMBER @desc Years the sum has been held to the credit of the estate before 1 March
      `the Public Trustee knows of someone entitled or claiming` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Public Trustee has any information of a person entitled in distribution, or claiming to be
      `the sum` IS A NUMBER @desc The unclaimed sum to the credit of the estate, in dollars
      `it has been advertised twice 14 days apart` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has been advertised as s 45(2) requires
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May money held for me go to the Consolidated Account` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a beneficiary of an estate or trust the Public Trustee administers` THEN `yes if` (`May the sum go to the Consolidated Account` `years the sum has been held` `the Public Trustee knows of someone entitled or claiming` `the sum` `it has been advertised twice 14 days apart`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a person owed money by someone who has died`

§§§ `s 11 -- a creditor against the Public Trustee`

@export As a creditor applying to administer the estate, may I be preferred to the Public Trustee (Public Trustee Act 1941 (WA) s 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the creditor proves to the Court it would be more beneficial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied the creditor administering would benefit the estate more
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As a creditor may I be preferred to the Public Trustee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am owed money by someone who has died` THEN `yes if` (NOT (`Is the Public Trustee preferred to a creditor` `the creditor proves to the Court it would be more beneficial`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
